WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.860
(upbeat music)

00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:03.240
- So usually when I have
a first time volunteer

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.690
come and be a part of a class
and their face says it all.

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:08.607
They're like, "Oh my gosh,
that was the coolest thing

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:10.080
"I've ever been a part of."

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.799
'Cause it's just a joyful place.

00:00:12.799 --> 00:00:15.966
(bright upbeat music)

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:30.500
My name is Lauren Beasley
and I'm the founder

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.130
and executive director
of Move Inclusive Dance

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:35.680
Move Inclusive Dance is a
dance studio for everyone,

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.140
no matter their ability level.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:40.030
But I took my first dance class
when I was three years old.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:43.920
From that point on, it was
pretty much my everything.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.680
For me, not only was it,
you know, a fun activity,

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.330
but it was the place where I could go

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:52.540
and know that it was safe for
me to express my emotions,

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:55.920
be myself, and it was just
really a creative outlet.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.380
It was way more than just learning steps.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.650
Not everyone loves to dance,
but a lot of people do.

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:02.500
It's the same for people
with disabilities, right?

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.840
Why wouldn't there be a
place that they could go

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:07.350
take a dance class like I can?

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:09.040
They don't have that opportunity.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:11.650
And because it was so
transformative in my life,

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:14.530
I felt like it was my duty at that point

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:15.763
to make it possible.

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:20.240
When we start the choreography,

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.760
what's the very first thing
that we do in this combo?

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:28.760
Yes Emma show them we slide and we party.

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.580
We slide and we party.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:34.400
(camera clicks)

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.960
When I'm driving to the studio,

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:38.910
I'm probably planning
my classes for the day.

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:41.540
One of the things that is different

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:43.420
when you're teaching adaptive dance,

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:46.410
you wanna have a good solid plan,

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:50.770
but you also have to be prepared
for literally anything else

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:53.700
to happen just in case,
plan A doesn't really go,

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:56.729
as I thought, and you just gotta be ready

00:01:56.729 --> 00:01:58.393
to move on your toes like that.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:01.900
- I oversee all of the programming here

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:03.380
at Move Inclusive Dance.

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:07.020
I'm seeing if all the students
are getting their needs met.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.450
You have to get to know the student

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:13.040
in order to understand
exactly what they need.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:15.660
And that's what inclusion is all about.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:18.510
It's a dance class, but it's adapting

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:21.120
to whoever is coming through the doors.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:23.490
- We've tailored everything that we do

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:26.190
everything in the building,
every part of our curriculum

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:29.830
to be adapted for people
with special needs,

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:32.280
but at the same time,
people without special needs

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.782
are also welcome in the classes too.

00:02:33.782 --> 00:02:35.123
Yes we go.

00:02:35.123 --> 00:02:36.456
One one and two.

00:02:37.392 --> 00:02:38.793
One one and two.

00:02:38.793 --> 00:02:42.230
From here, we do a little kick
combination with our feet.

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:43.780
So if you're doing the
feet, it'll look like this

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:47.300
you go kick forward, take
sides and then change it up.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:51.630
Again, go forward and side
and then change it up.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.660
And if you're just doing the upper body,

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:54.721
you're gonna kinda just like...

00:02:54.721 --> 00:02:55.882
(vocalizing)

00:02:55.882 --> 00:02:59.040
Switch sides, (vocalizing), switch sides.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.660
- Building a better
community and a better place

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:02.743
is the ultimate goal.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:07.010
- No matter where you come from,

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:10.170
what ability level you have, you fit here.

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:13.850
We're going to make dance work for you.

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:16.960
But when things shut down due to COVID,

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.700
we immediately had to pivot.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:21.733
And so we took things
to a virtual setting.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:25.870
Can someone tell me
what's improv dance is?

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:27.620
Raise your hand if you know.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:32.140
- It is the way you just
dance without any instruction.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.980
- Yes, it's when you dance
without any instruction,

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.310
that's a really good description of it.

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:39.160
You know, it's definitely not
the same as being in person.

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:44.110
But what I've found is that
people right now more than ever

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:45.890
are craving connection.

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:47.340
Our students that are
doing the zoom classes,

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:49.700
they love their weekly sessions

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:51.350
because they get to see their friends.

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:53.760
We've had a handful of
students that have participated

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:56.080
from out of state because
we're doing it online, right?

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:57.650
So you can really join from anywhere.

00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:00.980
And that's been a really,
really cool thing to see

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:04.620
because it's just opened our program up.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:08.500
It just requires a lot of
energy from me as the teacher.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:12.513
I am like worn out by the end
of one of our virtual classes.

00:04:13.397 --> 00:04:15.770
(upbeat music)

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:17.007
Let's do this, just follow me.

00:04:17.007 --> 00:04:20.174
(bright upbeat music)

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:47.040
We use dance to get our message out there.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:47.873
But at the end of the day,

00:04:47.873 --> 00:04:51.140
we just want people to
be open to one another,

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:53.934
love one another and be positive.

00:04:53.934 --> 00:04:57.101
(bright upbeat music)

